metadata.meta.description.Icon=The texture to display on the title banner in level selection representing the map.\nRelative to Gui atlas folder.
metadata.meta.description.Interlude=Whether the map is an interlude chapter. No B-sides, deaths aren't counted.
metadata.meta.description.CompleteScreenName=The texture used for the complete screen after beating the level.
metadata.meta.description.TitleBaseColor=The base colour of the title banner in level selection.
metadata.meta.description.TitleAccentColor=The colour of the additional text of the title banner and its accent in level selection.
metadata.meta.description.TitleTextColor=The colour of the main text of the title banner in level selection.
metadata.meta.description.Dreaming=Whether Madeline starts the map dreaming. Changes the appearance of the Stars background.
metadata.meta.description.ColorGrade=The global tinting of the map. Custom colour grades are relative to modRoot/Graphics/ColorGrading/.
metadata.meta.description.DarknessAlpha=The alpha value used for darkness. Defaults to 0.05.
metadata.meta.description.BloomBase=The base bloom level. Defaults to 0.0.
metadata.meta.description.BloomStrength=The strength of the bloom. Defaults to 1.0.
metadata.meta.description.CoreMode=The starting core mode (fire or ice). Can be changed in-game using core mode toggles.
metadata.meta.description.CassetteSong=The song played in the cassette room.
metadata.meta.description.IntroType=The way you enter the first room upon starting the map.
metadata.meta.description.Wipe=The animation that plays when the player respawns.\nExample use cases from the game.\n Curtain - Prologue\n Angled - Forsaken City\n Dream - Old Site\n KeyDoor - Celestial Resort\n Wind - Golden Ridge\n Drop - Mirror Temple\n Fall - Reflection\n Mountain - Summit\n Heart - Core\n Fade - Cutscenes\n Spotlight - Cutscenes
metadata.meta.description.AnimatedTiles=The XML file to use for custom Animated Tiles. Relative to mod root, temporarily used in place of the vanilla XML.
metadata.meta.description.ForegroundTiles=The XML file to use for custom Foreground Tiles. Relative to mod root, temporarily used in place of the vanilla XML.
metadata.meta.description.BackgroundTiles=The XML file to use for custom Background Tiles. Relative to mod root, temporarily used in place of the vanilla XML.
metadata.meta.description.Sprites=The XML file to use for custom Sprites. Relative to mod root, merged with the vanilla XML.
metadata.meta.description.Portraits=The XML file to use for custom Portraits. Relative to mod root, temporarily used in place of the vanilla XML.
metadata.meta.description.OverrideASideMeta=Whether to override the metadata of the A-Side.
metadata.meta.description.PostcardSoundID=The postcard sound to use. Leave empty for default.\nExamples: 1, 2, 3, csides.
# From side.meta.mode
metadata.mode.attribute.IgnoreLevelAudioLayerData=Ignore Room Layers
metadata.mode.attribute.Inventory=Starting Inventory
metadata.mode.attribute.StartLevel=Starting Room
metadata.mode.attribute.HeartIsEnd=End Level on Heart
metadata.mode.attribute.SeekerSlowdown=Seeker Slowdown
metadata.mode.attribute.TheoInBubble=Theo In Booster
metadata.mode.attribute.CoreModeIceTileOverlay=Core Mode Ice Tile Overlay
metadata.mode.description.IgnoreLevelAudioLayerData=Whether the layer data set on individual rooms should be ignored.
metadata.mode.description.Inventory=Your inventory starting the map. Changes the player's abilities.\n Prologue: 0 dashes, Dream blocks disabled, wearing a backpack, ground refills enabled\n Default: 1 dash, Dream blocks enabled, wearing a backpack, ground refills enabled\n OldSite: 1 dash, Dream blocks disabled, wearing a backpack, ground refills enabled\n CH6End: 2 dashes, Dream blocks enabled, wearing a backpack, ground refills enabled\n TheSummit: 2 dashes, Dream blocks enabled, not wearing a backpack, ground refills enabled\n Core: 2 dashes, Dream blocks enabled, wearing a backpack, ground refills disabled\n Farewell: 1 dash, Dream blocks enabled, not wearing a backpack, ground refills enabled
metadata.mode.description.StartLevel=The room to start the map in. By default, it will pick the room closest to absolute (0, 0).
metadata.mode.description.HeartIsEnd=Whether collecting a heart counts as the end of the level. The easiest way to end a level.
metadata.mode.description.SeekerSlowdown=Whether Seekers should be able to slow down time when attacking the player.
metadata.mode.description.TheoInBubble=Whether player is allowed to hold crystal Theo and other holdables while in a booster.
metadata.mode.description.CoreModeIceTileOverlay=Whether ice core mode should show overlay tiles.
